From 58df3f895217accff56d3a367a46ee4f6609d6bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 05:43:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] runbook 4.1b duty 3: a named collision is decided by
 MECHANISM READ + THREE ARMS (theirs / ours / union), never by one number -
 President 2026-09-02

---
 UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md b/UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md
index fa38e08ee..4fa864f2f 100644
--- a/UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md
+++ b/UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md
@@ -231,6 +231,18 @@ Two duties on EVERY bump/ingest, and the second is scoped tightly on his order:
      the targeted before/after (perf and/or quality, from OUR baseline) for that surface only.
    The collision list, empty or not, is a REQUIRED line in the bump report — "no intersections" is
    a checked claim, not an assumption.
+3. **A named collision is decided by MECHANISM + THREE ARMS, never by one number** (President 2026-09-02:
+   "replacing the thing with their thing just by sheer performance test is blind - maybe they don't include
+   something ours has which would also benefit theirs"). For every named collision:
+   - READ both deltas first and write, in the bump report, one paragraph per side: what upstream's change
+     does and why, what ours does and why, and whether the two mechanisms overlap, stack, or conflict.
+   - BENCH three arms on the seated line, counterbalanced: (a) upstream alone, (b) ours alone (the pre-bump
+     baseline), (c) the UNION = ours rebased on top of theirs. Quality gate on every arm.
+   - ADOPT the union when it is best. If upstream-alone beats the union, NAME the mechanism by which ours hurts
+     on top of theirs before dropping ours, and bank ours as a documented take with the configuration it still
+     wins on (a win is a win - it may be the answer for another format, width, or model). If the union loses
+     for an unknown reason, that is an open finding, not a drop.
+   - Never adopt or drop on the number alone; the report must carry the paragraph and the three arms.
 
 ### 4.2 It builds — the THREE-flag configure
 
